;aerostar4l.car.car;My 2008 Ford Aerostar Concept;This file includes describtive comments for most of the parameters.;If you still don't understand a parameter, just leave it unchangend.;these are for the car selection screen;a string with the name of the carcarName "Aerostar Sport Concept Supercharged"year 2008;displacement in litresdisplacement 4.2;---aerodynamics;the car's frontal air resitance.;this equals cw*S, where cw is the coefficient of friction ;and S is the frontal area of the car in square meters.;A modern sports car might have values as low as 0.6 for thisfrontAirResistance 1.1;air resistance of the side and top areas of the car.;these values are not that important to be very exact.sideAirResistance 2.0topAirResistance 1.0;used to simulate spoilers;negative values are downforce, positive values are upforcefrontLift -0.0rearLift -0.0;---chassis;Car's mass in kgmass 1530;Car's momentum of inertia around the x,y and z axis.;Meassured in kg*m^2;For those not into physics that much, inertia specifies the car's;initial resistance to get rotationally accelerated around it's axis. Smaller, lighter;cars have much lower values here. A formula-1 car might have an inertia;around the y-axis af about 750 kg*m^2, whereas a big station wagon may have;4000 kg*m^2. lower values result in better cornering abilitiesinertia {3400,3900,1100};The car's center of gravity.;This vector (as all the others that may follow) uses the following;coordinate system: X points to the right, Y points up and Z points to the front.;Coordinates are in meters.;The lower the CG, the better the cars handling.;Also, the further the CG is to the rear of the car, the more the car will tend;to oversteer in corners, making it much harder to handle. If your car uncontrollably;spins out in the rear a lot, try moving the CG further to the front.massCenter {0.0,0.813,0.4};An approximation of the car's borders, used for collision detection.;More than two boxes can be used, but if too many are used, performance ;may degrade. Each box is defined by 8 edges (top/front/right to bottom/rear/left).;number of collision boxesnumCollBoxes 1;a list of the collision boxes used, in this case only one;(the vw bus can be aproximated quite well with a single box)# 0coll.tfr {0.955,1.9,2.25}coll.tfl {-0.955,1.9,2.25}coll.trr {0.955,1.9,-2.25}coll.trl {-0.955,1.9,-2.25}coll.bfr {0.955,0.275,2.25}coll.bfl {-0.955,0.275,2.25}coll.brr {0.955,0.275,-2.25}coll.brl {-0.955,0.275,-2.25};---graphics;Model used to represent the car.model "Aerostar.mdl";Model used to represent the car's interior.;The VW bus has no interior graphics, so we just pass "null.mdl"interiorModel "null.mdl";Position of driver modeldriverPos {0.45,0.9,0.3};Position of the steering wheelsteeringWheelPos {0.45,1.0,0.9};Angle of the steering wheelsteeringWheelAngle 15;Number of turns, lock-to-lock.steeringWheelTurns 3.5;Model used to represent the steering wheelsteeringWheelModel "null.mdl"

numColors 10
# 0
colors {1,0,0}

# 1
colors {0,0,1}

# 2
colors {0,1,0}

# 3
colors {0,0,0}

# 4
colors {1,1,1}

# 5
colors {0.5,0.25,0}

# 6
colors {0.5,0.5,0.5}

# 7
colors {0,0.5,1}

# 8
colors {1,0.5,0}

# 9
colors {1,1,0}


;Position of left and right exhaust ends. For a car with only;one exhaust pipe, use the same coordinates for both.exhaust1Pos {-0.45,0.4,-2.3}exhaust2Pos {-0.45,0.4,-2.3};The lower this value, the more the car's exhaust will spit out banging noises and flames;Normally this should be off for street legal cars, but my vw bus has a broken exhaust ;-);just remove this line to turn this off.;Position of license plates;for network player namesfrontLicensePlatePos {0,0.55,2.3}rearLicensePlatePos {0,1.0,-2.2};--engine;Car's maximal power in Watts.;One hp equals 745.69987 Watts.power 200000;Car's maximal torque in Nm.;One lb-ft equals 1.35628105 Nm.torque 461;RPM values for the power and torque ratings.powerRPM 5250.0torqueRPM 3000.0;Engines idle RPMidleRPM 750.0jerkRPM 450;RPM delimtermaxRPM 5500.0;Engines Inertia in kg*m^2.;The higher this value is, the longer the engine takes to spin up.engineInertia 0.15;currently unusedengineFriction 100;engine sound sampleengineSample "enginemuffled copy.wav"hallSample "hallnormal2.wav"zeroRPMSoundGain 0.8fullRPMSoundGain 1.0zeroThrottleSoundGain 0.5fullThrottleSoundGain 1.1zeroRPMSoundPitch 0.4fullRPMSoundPitch 1.5zeroThrottleSoundPitch 0.8fullThrottleSoundPitch 1.0;---suspension;These determines the strength of the car's shock absorbers.supsensionFriction 900damperStrength 22000;sway Bars will cause the car to tilt less in corners. The higher these values,;the less the car will tilt to the side when corneringfrontSwayBar 12000rearSwayBar 18000;---drivetrain;The ratio of the final drive gear in the car's differential.finalDriveRatio 4.56;The maximum amount of torque the car's clutch can transfer (in Nm).maxClutchTorqueTransfer 1100;this factor is used to simulate limited slip differentials.;0 means free differential. the higher the value, the more differential locking.;values around 100 seem to get realistic limited slip differentials.differentialLockCoefficient 110;For automatic transmission: When to shift up and downshiftUpRPM 4500.0shiftDownRPM 2800.0;Time it takes to shift gears in secondsgearSwitchTime 0.4;Number of gears, including reverse and neutral.numGears 7;The gear ratios# 0gearRatios -3.72# 1gearRatios 0# 2gearRatios 3.72# 3gearRatios 2.20# 4gearRatios 1.50# 5gearRatios 1.00# 6
gearRatios 0.79;---wheels;number of wheels (theoretically you could make vehicles with numWheels!=4. This has not been tested and might cause troubles, though).numWheels 4;front left wheel# 0;Wheel's positionwheels.pos {-0.81,0.375,1.50};Wheel's inertia in kg*m^2.wheels.inertia 2.2;Fraction of engine power lead to this wheel.;0, as the bus is rear-wheel drivenwheels.powered .15;Friction caused by rotating the wheel in Nm.wheels.friction 11;Maximal steering angle of this wheel in radians.wheels.maxAngle 0.50;Suspension travel of this wheel in meters.wheels.maxSuspension 0.2;Wheel's radius in meters.wheels.radius 0.34;Torque of the brakes on this wheel (in Nm).wheels.braked 4000.0;How much of the braking torque is generated by pulling the handbrake (between 0 and 1).wheels.handbraked 0.0;model used to represent the wheel;we didn't supply a custom model for the wheel, so i'll use one built into the game,wheels.model "wheel-classic-disc.mdl";width of the wheel;wider wheels have better grip characteristics.;you might want to use wider wheels at the rear axle if the car tends to oversteer too much.wheels.width 0.265wheels.texture 4;front right wheel# 1wheels.pos {0.81,0.375,1.50}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.15wheels.friction 11wheels.maxAngle 0.50wheels.maxSuspension 0.2wheels.radius 0.34wheels.braked 4000.0wheels.handbraked 0.0wheels.model "wheel-classic-disc.mdl"wheels.width 0.265wheels.texture 4;rear left wheel# 2wheels.pos {-0.79,0.375,-1.36}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.3wheels.friction 11wheels.maxAngle 0.0wheels.maxSuspension 0.2wheels.radius 0.34wheels.braked 1500.0wheels.handbraked 1.0wheels.model "wheel-classic.mdl"wheels.width 0.265wheels.texture 4;rear right wheel# 3wheels.pos {0.79,0.375,-1.36}wheels.inertia 2.2wheels.powered 0.3wheels.friction 11wheels.maxAngle 0.0wheels.maxSuspension 0.2wheels.radius 0.34wheels.braked 1500.0wheels.handbraked 1.0wheels.model "wheel-classic.mdl"wheels.width 0.265wheels.texture 4;---lights;number of lights on the carnumLights 12# 0;the light's positionlights.pos {-0.82,2.00,2.30};direction the light is pointing tolights.dir {0,-0.1,1};RGB color of the lightlights.rgb {1,1,1};light type: either 0 for a glowing dot, 1 for a light cone;(visible at night only) or 2 for a dot which reflects on wet streets.lights.type 1;lights size, - length of light cone, or diameter of dotlights.size 30;what is the light used for:;0x01: normal driving light. ;0x08: reverse gear light.;0x10: brake light;0x20: left indicator;0x40: right indicatorlights.onFlags 0x01;tell the light to turn OFF, when one of the above mentioned lights turns on.lights.offFlags 0x00# 1lights.pos {0.82,2.00,2.30}lights.dir {0,-0.1,1}lights.rgb {1,1,1}lights.type 1lights.size 30lights.onFlags 0x01lights.offFlags 0x00# 2lights.pos {-0.75,1.10,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {0.8,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.2lights.onFlags 0x01lights.offFlags 0x00# 3lights.pos {0.75,1.10,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {0.8,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.2lights.onFlags 0x01lights.offFlags 0x00# 4lights.pos {-0.7,0.8,2.2}lights.dir {0,0,1}lights.rgb {1,1,1}lights.type 0lights.size 0.6lights.onFlags 0x01lights.offFlags 0x00# 5lights.pos {0.7,0.8,2.2}lights.dir {0,0,1}lights.rgb {1,1,1}lights.type 0lights.size 0.6lights.onFlags 0x01lights.offFlags 0x00# 6lights.pos {-0.3,0.5,2.3}lights.dir {0,0,1}lights.rgb {1,1,1}lights.type 0lights.size 0.5lights.onFlags 0x00lights.offFlags 0x00# 7lights.pos {0.0,1.75,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {1,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.18lights.onFlags 0x10lights.offFlags 0x00# 8lights.pos {-0.75,1.10,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {1,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.18lights.onFlags 0x10lights.offFlags 0x00# 9lights.pos {0.75,1.10,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {1,0,0}lights.type 2lights.size 0.18lights.onFlags 0x10lights.offFlags 0x00# 10lights.pos {-0.75,1.02,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {0.8,0.8,0.8}lights.type 0lights.size 0.3lights.onFlags 0x08lights.offFlags 0x00# 11lights.pos {0.75,1.02,-2.20}lights.dir {0,0,-1}lights.rgb {0.8,0.8,0.8}lights.type 0lights.size 0.3lights.onFlags 0x08lights.offFlags 0x00